Subject: Two Peepholes That Remove Dead Dispatches

What this does
  Two transformations in resolve_labels that delete executed instructions
  without adding an opcode or changing the bytecode format:
  `dup put_x_check(n) drop` becomes `put_x_check(n)`, and `lnot` in front of a
  conditional branch becomes the inverted branch.

Why we need it
  The TDZ-checked stores have no set_x form, so the existing
  `dup put_x(n) drop -> put_x(n)` peephole cannot match them and every
  `let`/`const` assignment used as a statement kept its dup and its drop.
  Separately, `!x` in front of an `if` ran a ToBoolean and a branch where the
  branch alone does the same work.

What it adds
  Neither transformation changes what is observable. `dup put_x_check(n) drop`
  stores one value and consumes one net reference, exactly as put_x_check(n)
  alone does, and the TDZ check still runs before any store, so the same
  ReferenceError is raised at the same point. `lnot` followed by a branch only
  ever consumed one value and branched on its truthiness, and ToBoolean runs no
  JavaScript, so the branch performs the same conversion, inversion and free.
  No opcode is added or retired, BC_VERSION is unchanged, and the precompiled
  built-in blobs are not regenerated because the format does not move.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

